<title>NETHERLANDS: REED-ELSEVIER TO BUY CHILTON BUSINESS.</title>
<headline>REED-ELSEVIER TO BUY CHILTON BUSINESS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Dutch publishing group Reed-Elsevier said on Monday it was to acquire Chilton Business Group for $447 million.  </p>
<p>Reed Elsevier said in a statement it was buying the U.S. business publisher Chilton, a unit of The Walt Disney Company , for cash. Completion of the deal, subject to U.S. government clearances, was expected by the end of July.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect the acquisition to be earnings accretive for Reed International and Elsevier shareholders from the outset,&quot; the statement said.</p>
